---
// site/src/pages/terms.astro
import '../styles/global.css';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import GoogleAnalytics from '../components/GoogleAnalytics.astro';

const BASE = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const SITE = 'https://ezterm.zerosandones.us';
const REPO = 'https://github.com/ZerosAndOnesLLC/ezTerm';
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="dark">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="referrer" content="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" />
    <title>ezTerm Terms of Use</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Terms of use for ezTerm, the free, open-source SSH client. Provided as-is under GPLv3, without warranty of any kind." />
    <link rel="canonical" href={`${SITE}/terms/`} />
    <meta property="og:type" content="article" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="ezTerm Terms of Use" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="ezTerm is provided as-is under GPLv3, without warranty of any kind." />
    <meta property="og:url" content={`${SITE}/terms/`} />
    <meta property="og:image" content={`${SITE}/og.png`} />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="ezTerm" />
    <meta property="og:locale" content="en_US" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="twitter:title" content="ezTerm Terms of Use" />
    <meta name="twitter:description" content="ezTerm is provided as-is under GPLv3, without warranty of any kind." />
    <meta name="twitter:image" content={`${SITE}/og.png`} />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href={`${BASE}ezterm-icon.png`} />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href={`${BASE}ezterm-icon-192.png`} />
    <link rel="manifest" href={`${BASE}manifest.json`} />
    <GoogleAnalytics />
  </head>
  <body class="bg-site-bg text-site-fg">
    <header class="border-b border-site-border">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-4 flex items-center justify-between">
        <a href={BASE} class="flex items-center font-bold tracking-tight">
          <img src={`${BASE}ezterm-icon.png`} alt="ezTerm" width="40" height="40" class="h-10 w-auto" />
        </a>
        <nav class="flex items-center gap-6 text-sm text-site-fg-muted">
          <a href={`${BASE}docs/`} class="hover:text-site-fg">Docs</a>
          <a href={`${BASE}screenshots/`} class="hover:text-site-fg">Screenshots</a>
          <a href={`${BASE}changelog/`} class="hover:text-site-fg">Changelog</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/ZerosAndOnesLLC/ezTerm" class="hover:text-site-fg">GitHub</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-12">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-2">Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="text-site-fg-muted mb-10">Effective date: August 20, 2026</p>

      <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none">
        <p>
          These terms apply to the <strong>ezTerm</strong> desktop application and the
          <strong>ezterm.zerosandones.us</strong> website, operated by Zeros and Ones LLC
          ("we", "us"). By downloading, installing, or using ezTerm, or by using this website,
          you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, do not use the software or the site.
        </p>

        <h2>License</h2>
        <p>
          ezTerm is free, open-source software licensed under the
          <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>GNU General Public License, version 3 (GPLv3)</a>.
          The GPLv3 governs your rights to use, copy, modify, and redistribute the software.
          Nothing in these terms restricts the rights the GPLv3 grants you; these terms
          supplement it with respect to the website, downloads, and your use of the software.
        </p>

        <h2>Disclaimer of warranty</h2>
        <p>
          TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, THE SOFTWARE AND THE WEBSITE ARE
          PROVIDED <strong>"AS IS"</strong> AND <strong>"AS AVAILABLE"</strong>, WITHOUT WARRANTY
          OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF
          MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, TITLE, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT. WE DO
          NOT WARRANT THAT THE SOFTWARE WILL BE ERROR-FREE, SECURE, OR UNINTERRUPTED, THAT DEFECTS
          WILL BE CORRECTED, OR THAT THE SOFTWARE IS FREE OF VULNERABILITIES. THE ENTIRE RISK AS
          TO THE QUALITY AND PERFORMANCE OF THE SOFTWARE IS WITH YOU. SHOULD THE SOFTWARE PROVE
          DEFECTIVE, YOU ASSUME THE COST OF ALL NECESSARY SERVICING, REPAIR, OR CORRECTION.
        </p>

        <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, IN NO EVENT SHALL ZEROS AND ONES LLC,
          ITS MEMBERS, CONTRIBUTORS, OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY DIRECT, INDIRECT,
          INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, EXEMPLARY, CONSEQUENTIAL, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES WHATSOEVER —
          INCLUDING WITHOUT LIMITATION LOSS OF DATA, LOSS OF CREDENTIALS, DATA BEING RENDERED
          INACCURATE, UNAUTHORIZED ACCESS TO YOUR SYSTEMS, BUSINESS INTERRUPTION, LOST PROFITS,
          OR FAILURE OF THE SOFTWARE TO OPERATE WITH ANY OTHER SOFTWARE — ARISING OUT OF OR IN
          CONNECTION WITH THE USE OF OR INABILITY TO USE THE SOFTWARE OR THE WEBSITE, HOWEVER
          CAUSED AND UNDER ANY THEORY OF LIABILITY (CONTRACT, TORT, NEGLIGENCE, STRICT LIABILITY,
          OR OTHERWISE), EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES. WHERE LIABILITY
          CANNOT BE EXCLUDED, IT IS LIMITED TO THE AMOUNT YOU PAID FOR THE SOFTWARE, WHICH IS
          ZERO. SOME JURISDICTIONS DO NOT ALLOW THE EXCLUSION OR LIMITATION OF CERTAIN WARRANTIES
          OR DAMAGES, SO SOME OF THE ABOVE MAY NOT APPLY TO YOU; IN THAT CASE, LIABILITY IS
          LIMITED TO THE GREATEST EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW.
        </p>

        <h2>Your responsibilities</h2>
        <p>
          ezTerm is a tool for connecting to remote systems. You are solely responsible for:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Only connecting to systems you own or are authorized to access, and complying with
            all applicable laws and the policies of the systems and networks you use.
          </li>
          <li>
            Safeguarding your master password, credentials, and keys. If you lose your master
            password, your vault cannot be recovered — by you or by us.
          </li>
          <li>
            Maintaining backups of your data. Verify host key fingerprints and exercise your own
            judgment when accepting new hosts.
          </li>
          <li>
            Anything you do on remote systems through ezTerm, including commands executed and
            files transferred or deleted.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Third-party services and software</h2>
        <p>
          Updates are distributed via GitHub Releases, and the optional X server component
          (VcXsrv) is downloaded from SourceForge. These are independent services with their own
          terms; we are not responsible for their availability or content. VcXsrv is separate
          software with its own license and is not part of ezTerm.
        </p>

        <h2>Indemnification</h2>
        <p>
          You agree to indemnify and hold harmless Zeros and Ones LLC and the project's
          contributors from any claims, damages, or expenses (including reasonable attorneys'
          fees) arising from your use or misuse of the software, your violation of these terms,
          or your violation of any law or third-party right.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these terms from time to time; changes take effect when posted on this
          page with an updated effective date. Continued use of the software or site after
          changes are posted constitutes acceptance. The full history of this document is
          available in the <a href={REPO}>public repository</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms? Open an issue on
          <a href={`${REPO}/issues`}>GitHub</a>, or use the channels in our
          <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/SECURITY.md`}>security policy</a> for anything sensitive.
        </p>

        <p>
          See also our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </main>

    <SiteFooter />
  </body>
</html>
